```

In this example, we apply a lambda function to all elements of the list `lst[:-2]`, which excludes the last two sublists `[9, 10]`. The lambda function returns a tuple of the element and its square value.

The `map()` function then applies the lambda function to each element of the list and returns a map object, which is converted to a list using the `list()` function. The resulting list is a nested list of tuples as required.
