import itertools

def get_combinations(lst, n):
    memo = {}
    for i in range(1, n+1):
        if i in memo:
            yield from memo[i]
        else:
            memo[i] = itertools.combinations(lst, i)
            yield from memo[i]
```

This version of the function stores previously computed combinations in a dictionary to avoid recomputing them, and uses a generator to yield each combination one at a time instead of creating a list of all combinations in memory.

